launchers.notes:
SINGLE-PLAYER render check. This is the only launcher for the unattended round.

It calls the staged Play launcher unchanged (1680 B on all 8 boxes, DIRLIST 2026-11-11). That launcher:
- calls %~dp0FLEETRES.BAT;
- writes HKLM\Software\Lonely Cat Games\Hidden and Dangerous Deluxe\Config with FLEETRES.EXE -reg: Display width/height = FR_W/FR_H, bitdepth 32 and Fullscreen 1. The engine has no fullscreen switch; 'resolution x y' only sizes a window;
- does cd /d to the tree root, because HDE.exe opens data\*.dta and Savegame\ relative to the working directory;
- runs start "" Bin\HDE.exe, then exit.

GAMERES VERIFY on .110, .184 and .240 (2026-11-11) confirms that all 3 launchers call FLEETRES and that the persisted Config already equals each box's target. No player name is set: single player has none. The Config key also keeps HDE.exe from spawning bin\iconfig.exe ('Cannot run IConfig.exe.').

Send NO keys or clicks during the check. To close the game: UIKEY ALT+F4, but only when WINLIST's foreground window is HDE.exe's IGraph_Window; otherwise PROCKILL. lanparty's kill already uses PROCKILL.

The attended host and join variants are in host_box and are deliberately not listed here.

